From a71257f935b794b294c2ed68e67484ca8fcf73a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS <claude.ai@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 19:24:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 106/114] core: add the public helper facade from ofono/misc.h

External drivers need to decode SIM GET RESPONSE data, look up elementary
file paths, format phone numbers and render the registration and access
technology enumerations. Sailfish exposes these as ofono_* wrappers over
helpers oFono keeps internal.

They have to live in oFono rather than in a separate library: every one of
them wraps a symbol the version script does not export, such as
sim_parse_2g_get_response(), sim_ef_db_get_path_2g(), encode_hex_own_buf()
and registration_tech_to_string(). A library outside the daemon could not
reach any of them.

ofono_decode_cbs_dcs_charset() is left out. It would require promoting
enum sms_charset as well, and no external driver calls it.

ofono_phone_number_to_string() uses g_strlcpy instead of Sailfish's
strncpy followed by explicit termination. Same truncation, same NUL, and
no warning about a copy that deliberately fills the buffer.

(cherry picked from commit 9a2d8d9df7f5d63c7252cea83a4de6f886de9e6f)
Upstream-Status: Pending
